36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The wall is single plasterboard. I can hear both sides of a call from my desk. Sound is the real barrier, not the door.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The last awkward conversation happened across the desks, in front of everyone. We went quiet for a fortnight. We need a place to speak without an audience.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,The invoices show sixty-eight thousand yen paid out last year. We are bleeding money for space we don't even use properly.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The quotes are in. Screen and table cost 141,000 yen. The kitchen setup is 96,000. I want the paper before we pick a side.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Servas,,"Since the sofa went in, unplanned talk only happens by the printer. The two who started in spring still barely know the rest of us.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the 141,000 yen for the meeting space is high, but the 96,000 for the kitchen is lower. However, the plasterboard wall means sound leaks either way.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, the wall is thin, but the real issue is the lack of privacy for difficult talks. We need a space where we can speak without an audience.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@May, sixty-eight thousand yen is a lot, but the lunch trip takes twenty-five minutes. We are paying for time we don't have.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the lunch trip is a time cost, not a capital one. I’m sticking with the quotes. We need the fit-out numbers before we debate daily habits.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Jonathan, the printer is a poor substitute for a room. We need a place where difficult things can be said without an audience.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Servas, the printer is a dead end. If we choose the kitchen, the noise will leak through that plasterboard wall anyway. We need to accept that trade-off.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, you’re right about the noise, but a kitchen doesn’t solve the silence. We need a room where hard conversations can happen without the whole office listening in.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, the 96,000 yen is cheaper, but the 25-minute lunch trip is a daily tax. We need to weigh the capital cost against the time we lose every day.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, I hear you, but time is not money in the ledger. I need the capital figures settled before we start calculating your daily commute.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, the twenty-five minutes is real, but the 96,000 yen is a one-time hit. I’d rather we stop paying for space we don’t use properly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the capital cost is settled. The real issue is that the plasterboard wall makes any private conversation impossible. We need to address the sound leakage before we choose a function.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, the wall is a fact, but the silence is the wound. We need a room where hard things can be said without an audience.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you’re ignoring the daily drain. Twenty-five minutes a day is hours lost. I need that time cost weighed against your capital figures.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, I am not ignoring it. I am refusing to let a commute dictate a capital expenditure. The quotes are the only hard facts we have.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Shunichi, the ledger is cold, but the room is warm. We must choose a purpose that heals the silence, not just balances the books.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
